WEBVTT

00:00:59.388 --> 00:01:00.932
But they've done more than that.

00:01:00.973 --> 00:01:04.310
They've created a culture of reporting
on your friends, your neighbors,

00:01:04.352 --> 00:01:05.478
even your own family.

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:07.230
And just a suspicion of being queer

00:01:07.230 --> 00:01:09.565
can result in these
life-threatening consequences.

00:01:09.607 --> 00:01:11.859
So as you might imagine,
under these conditions,

00:01:11.859 --> 00:01:15.196
many queer people are constantly
operating from a place of concern

00:01:15.238 --> 00:01:17.031
and fear about being outed.

00:01:17.406 --> 00:01:18.825
And if we're all in hiding,

00:01:18.825 --> 00:01:22.161
then how can we mobilize around issues
that impede our everyday lives

00:01:22.203 --> 00:01:24.080
or share resources in times of need?

00:01:24.122 --> 00:01:27.333
How can we create a space
where we can thrive?

00:01:28.084 --> 00:01:31.796
We hear a lot in the news lately
about social media and online platforms